# Per-example pipeline configuration for the "portainer" awesome-compose
# example.
#
# PREBUILT example: no Dockerfile in the entry, so PREBUILT_IMAGE names the
# registry reference the vendor compose file gives the target service and
# pipeline/build.sh pulls and re-tags it instead of building. See
# docs/methodology.md §12.
#
# Single-service example, and the only one whose dependency is the host's own
# Docker daemon rather than another container: it manages Docker through the
# bind-mounted /var/run/docker.sock. That mount is the example's whole point,
# so it is reproduced as upstream declares it — including for Slim's analysis
# run, which needs it for the API to answer at all.
EXAMPLE=portainer
COMPOSE_FILE=vendor/awesome-compose/portainer/compose.yaml
COMPOSE_SERVICE=portainer
PREBUILT_IMAGE=portainer/portainer-ce:alpine
IMAGE_NAME=dip-portainer
CONTAINER_PORT=9000
HOST_PORT=8115
HEALTH_PATH=/
HEALTH_EXPECT="portainer"
STARTUP_WAIT=15

EXTRA_PROBE_PATHS="/api/status /api/system/status"

# Slim-only: the Docker socket, restated as a plain mount because docker-slim
# starts its container outside compose. Absolute host path — pipeline/slim.sh
# treats a leading "/" as absolute rather than repo-relative.
APP_MOUNT="/var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock"

# Portainer initialises its database under /data (the portainer_data volume
# under compose, plain container filesystem under docker-slim).
SLIM_MOUNTS="dip-slim-scratch-portainer:/data"
# Paired with SLIM_MOUNTS above: mint's --exclude-mounts does not actually
# keep a mounted volume's contents out of the output image (verified), so the
# same path is also excluded by pattern. Both the directory and its contents,
# because leftover empty directories carry the analysis run's ownership.
SLIM_EXCLUDE_PATTERNS="/data /data/* /data/**"
